iTerm2:
- Download it from website
- Go to Settings > Preferences
- Set the load preferences from custom folder and set it to dotfiles/configs (where com.googlecode.iterm2.plist should be)
- For font and colourschemes, see below.

fzf:
- Just `brew install fzf`, the zsh config will source keybindings once the binary is available in the path.

Vim:
- You'll want to `brew install vim` instead of the provided one with macos as it's missing some features.

NeoVim:
- Had to follow https://peterbabic.dev/blog/install-pynvim-via-homebrew-properly/ to get the python provider working.
- New iterm colorschemes: https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim/tree/main/extras/iterm
